# Arc Summaries

![fSSEED_IntroQuest.drawio.png](fSSEED_IntroQuest.drawio.png)

***Core idea:*** The player gradually learns that emotional neutrality is a choice—one Alenawe must reckon with.

## The cover
Cover progression: recruitment (research cover) → small slips (operative language) → strained reports → protocol breach (courier) → contested association → delivered choice.

Purpose: show institutions as managed fictions, reveal that Alenawe performs a role for both the Thalmor and the player, and make her reporting choices an axis of agency.

## Possible play orders (summary)
- Ideal: MinQ1 → MajQ1 → DI → MinQ2 → MajQ2 — full ramp and maximum impact.
- Partial: DI can occur before MinQ1/MajQ1; quests adapt their framing (pre- or post-DI).
- Fallback: If MajQ1 never fires, DI supplies the forced-clarity beat and the arc still completes.

## Recruitment (brief)
- Normal: curious, intrigued by an alternate mode of power.
- Post-DI: guarded, suspicious; recruitment dialogue carries interlude weight. Still competent, but visibly stressed.

## MINOR QUEST 1 — Observation that slips (The Inquiry)
- Goal: plant the spine question — "How do you operate without institutional scaffolding?"
- Delivery: idle/dead-drop triggered at Affinity ≥ Tier 1 (Stability ≠ Liability).
- Beat: Alenawe slips into operative phrasing, self-corrects, player notices. No mechanical consequences—this logs a claim and invites further probing.

## MAJOR QUEST 1 — The Model Fails (summary)
- Gate: Affinity ≥ 21, Stability ≠ Liability, ~3 days after MinQ1.
- Goal: force a data point that contradicts her institutional model — the player solves a field problem in a way her procedure couldn't predict.
- Structure: dead-drop → field mission (radiant asset) → collision (her procedural approach vs. player's illegible method) → aftermath conversation where she recalculates.

## INTERLUDE — Diplomatic Immunity (summary)
- Trigger: DI event (main quest) or courier if recruited post-DI.
- Purpose: emotional model failure — authority acted emotionally and bypassed procedure; neutrality did not insulate. The courier/protocol breach signals the system broke its own rules.

## MINOR QUEST 2 — The Stakes (The Mentor)
- Trigger: ~3 days after the Interlude; dead-drop summons a hearing.
- Goal: system corrected; Mentor arrives to reassign her. She must argue to stay. This is the fork moment (protect Machine / self / truth / Dragonborn trajectory) and it reveals which heading she takes:
  • Professional justification → Path A (Reformer)
  • Request time to reclassify → Path C (Architect)
  • Can't articulate / simply chooses proximity → Path B (Independent)
- Player actions (support, intervene, stay silent, undermine) nudge the fork but do not decide for her.

## MAJOR QUEST 2 — Choosing a Frame That Holds (summary)
- Trigger: MinQ2 complete + ~5 days + Affinity ≥ Tier 2; delivered via dead-drop.
- Beat 1: she drafts an assessment (truth, reframe, or legible translation).
- Beat 2: field mission to prove that assessment — path-dependent gameplay
  • Path A (Contain): she directs the Dragonborn to behave as a contained asset; success lets her stay and operationalize the lie.
  • Path C (Align): she collaborates with the Dragonborn to demonstrate integration; success supports reclassification but invites institutional pushback.
  • Path B (Unleash): she uses the Dragonborn openly to prove illegibility; the system goes silent and scaffolding collapses.
- Beat 3: system response (dead-drop or courier) and final resolution; consequences and reward reflect which frame she chose.

## End states (condensed)
- Holding pattern: she stays useful and distant; the system persists.
- Individuation: she chooses proximity without necessity; she stands without scaffolding and the player receives a private, pragmatic reward.

## Late recruitment note
- If recruited post-DI, the arc still functions but reframes earlier beats as retrospective and shifts emotional weight into recruitment and MinQ1/MinQ2.

